Voting Unit (Unit A):
INCLUDED:  All full-time, regular part-time, and per diem registered nurses (RNs) providing direct patient care, employed by the Employer;

Also eligible to vote are all employees in the unit who have worked an average of 4 hours or more per week during the 13 weeks immediately preceding the eligibility date of the election. 

EXCLUDED: All other employees, educators, infection control RNs, nurse practitioners, case managers, performance improvement RNs, traveler RNs, RNs employed by registries or other agencies providing outside labor to the Employer, office clerical employees, managerial employees, confidential employees, guards, and supervisors (including Clinical Shift Supervisors or Permanent Charge Nurses) as defined in the Act.

INCLUDING: All full-time and regular part time components technicians, electricians, e-technicians, fabrication technicians, lift truck operators, M technicians, production machine operators, quality gage lab technicians, quality layout technicians, waste water technicians, HVAC technicians, PM filter/lubrication technicians, storeroom attendants, and team leaders-in-training employed by the Employer at its 1200 International Place, Danville, IL 61834 and 204 Eastgate Drive, Danville, IL 61834 facilities;

EXCLUDING: All office clerical employees, professional employees, employees supplied by a staffing agency, manufacturing process engineers, control engineers/electronic specialists, guards and supervisors as defined by the Act and all other employees.

Others permitted to vote: The parties have agreed that quality shop floor technicians, engineering technician coordinators, junior maintenance planners, logistics administrative assistants, and manufacturing engineering technicians may vote in the election but their ballots will be challenged since their eligibility has not been resolved.

Included: All full-time and part-time dietary aides and cooks employed by the Employer at its facility located at 1663 East Division Street, River Falls, Wisconsin;

Excluded: All registered nurses (RN’s), licensed practical nurses (LPN’s), office clerical employees, receptionists, temporary and on-call employees, guards and supervisors as defined in the Act, and all other classifications not expressly included in the bargaining unit.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for the petitioner, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing bargaining unit consisting of PRN nursing assistants, restorative nursing assistants, activity aides, housekeepers, laundry aides, janitors, and social service aides, currently represented by United Food and Commercial Workers Union Local 1189.  If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

Included:  All full-time and regular part-time Distribution Service Representative I, II and Senior;

Excluded:  Professionals, managers, and guards and supervisors as defined by the Act, as amended.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF ELECTRICAL WORKERS LOCAL 31, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing unit represented by INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF ELECTRICAL WORKERS LOCAL 31, as described in its current collective bargaining agreement with the Employer effective February 1, 2018, through April 30, 2020.  If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

All full-time and regular part-time Engineers, Assistant Engineers, Painters, and Gardeners who perform work at The Saint Paul Hotel located at 350 Market St., Saint Paul, Minnesota; 

excluding all other employees, managers, confidential employees, and guards and supervisors as defined by the Act, as amended.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for UNITE HERE Local 17, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing bargaining unit defined by the collective bargaining agreement between Morrissey Hospitality Companies, Inc. and Unite Here Union Local 17 AFL-CIO, which is currently represented by UNITE HERE Local 17. If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

INCLUDED:  All full-time and regular part-time drivers, driver/instructors, bus assistants, and maintenance technicians employed by the Employer at its facilities currently located at 16627 South Avalon Boulevard, Carson, California and 8555 Flower Street, Paramount, California;

EXCLUDED: All other employees, office clerical employees, professional employees, managerial employees, guards, and supervisors as defined in the Act.

However, all full-time and regular part-time maintenance administrators employed by the Employer at its facilities currently located at 16627 South Avalon Boulevard, Carson, California and 8555 Flower Street, Paramount, Californiaare are neither included in nor excluded from the bargaining unit covered by this certification, because the parties did not agree on the inclusion or exclusion of maintenance administrators, but agreed to vote them subject to challenge and resolution of their inclusion or exclusion was unnecessary because their ballots were not determinative of the election results.
